}}The '''2022 Wakefield Metropolitan District Council election''' took place on 5 May 2022 to elect members of [[Wakefield Council]]. This was on the same day as [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections]]. 21 of the 63 seats were up for election.<ref>{{cite web |title=Election timetable in England |url=https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/election-timetable-in-england/election-timetable-in-england#metropolitan-districts |website=GOV.UK |access-date=9 April 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

==Background==
Since its first election in 1973, [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] has always controlled [[Wakefield Council]], only falling below 60% of seats on 4 occasions (most recently in [[2010 Wakefield Metropolitan District Council election|2010]]).<ref>{{cite web |title=City of Wakefield Metropolitan District Council Election Results 1973-2012 |url=http://www.electionscentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/Wakefield-1973-2012.pdf |website=Elections Centre |access-date=12 April 2022 |page=24}}</ref> In the [[2021 Wakefield Metropolitan District Council election|2021 election]], Labour lost 6 seats with 45.1% of the vote, the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservatives]] gained 6 seats with 37.5%, the [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] gained 1 with 3.0%, and independents lost 1 with 2.1%

The seats up for election this year were last elected in [[2018 Wakefield Metropolitan District Council election|2018]]. In that election, Labour lost 1 seat with 51.7% of the vote, the Conservatives gained 4 with 34.0%, independents lost 1 with 3.9%, and [[UK Independence Party|UKIP]] lost both their seats up for election with 1.1%.

